Packed objects carry two safeguards against tools that do not know CodeView
packs: their .debug$T has its own signature, and their .drectve names a
sentinel symbol through /INCLUDE:, so that another linker fails with an error
naming it. LLD ignores the sentinel, and restoring an object removes both.

a.obj has no .drectve: packing adds one as its last section. b.obj has one,
ending with NUL padding: the directive goes before the padding.

RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t/orig
RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/cvpacks-src-a.yaml -o %t/orig/a.obj
RUN: %python %S/Inputs/cvpacks-add-drectve.py %S/Inputs/cvpacks-src-b.yaml \
RUN:   %t/b.yaml " /DEFAULTLIB:foo.lib"
RUN: yaml2obj %t/b.yaml -o %t/orig/b.obj

RUN: llvm-cvpack pack --out-dir=%t/stage %t/orig/a.obj %t/orig/b.obj
RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PACK < %t/stage/cvpacks.json
PACK-NOT: "packs": []

RUN: llvm-readobj --file-headers %t/orig/a.obj | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=COUNT-ORIG
RUN: llvm-readobj --file-headers %t/stage/a.obj | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=COUNT-PACKED
COUNT-ORIG: SectionCount: 10
COUNT-PACKED: SectionCount: 11

RUN: llvm-readobj --string-dump=.drectve %t/stage/a.obj | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DIRECTIVE-A
DIRECTIVE-A: /INCLUDE:__cvpack_object_needs_lld_link_or_cvpack_materialize
RUN: llvm-readobj --string-dump=.drectve %t/stage/b.obj | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DIRECTIVE-B
DIRECTIVE-B: /DEFAULTLIB:foo.lib /INCLUDE:__cvpack_object_needs_lld_link_or_cvpack_materialize

RUN: llvm-readobj --codeview %t/stage/a.obj | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MAGIC
MAGIC:      CodeViewTypes [
MAGIC-NEXT:   Section: .debug$T
MAGIC-NEXT:   Magic: 0x31505643
MAGIC:        TypeLeafKind: LF_CVPACK_LIST (0x1700)

Staged objects, with either kind of directive edit, round-trip through obj2yaml
and yaml2obj.
RUN: obj2yaml %t/stage/a.obj -o %t/a.staged.yaml
RUN: obj2yaml %t/stage/b.obj -o %t/b.staged.yaml
RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=YAML-A < %t/a.staged.yaml
RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=YAML-B < %t/b.staged.yaml
YAML-A: Kind: AddedDirectiveSection
YAML-B: Kind: Directive
RUN: yaml2obj %t/a.staged.yaml -o %t/a.staged.obj
RUN: yaml2obj %t/b.staged.yaml -o %t/b.staged.obj
RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-files-equal.py %t/stage/a.obj %t/a.staged.obj
RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-files-equal.py %t/stage/b.obj %t/b.staged.obj

Restoring removes the directive and the added section, and the signature.
RUN: llvm-cvpack materialize %t/stage/a.obj -o %t/a.restored.obj
RUN: llvm-cvpack materialize %t/stage/b.obj -o %t/b.restored.obj
RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-files-equal.py %t/orig/a.obj %t/a.restored.obj
RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-files-equal.py %t/orig/b.obj %t/b.restored.obj

Packing packed objects again recognizes them by their signature and leaves
them unchanged.
RUN: llvm-cvpack pack --pack-path=%t/stage --out-dir=%t/stage2 \
RUN:   %t/stage/a.obj %t/stage/b.obj
RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-files-equal.py %t/stage/a.obj %t/stage2/a.obj
RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-files-equal.py %t/stage/b.obj %t/stage2/b.obj

LLD links the packed objects without resolving the sentinel, and gives the same
PDB type stream as a link of the originals.
RUN: env LLD_IN_TEST=1 lld-link /noentry /dll /nodefaultlib /debug \
RUN:   /out:%t/packed.dll %t/stage/a.obj %t/stage/b.obj
RUN: env LLD_IN_TEST=1 lld-link /noentry /dll /nodefaultlib /debug \
RUN:   /out:%t/orig.dll %t/orig/a.obj %t/orig/b.obj
RUN: llvm-pdbutil dump -types %t/orig.pdb > %t/orig-types.txt
RUN: llvm-pdbutil dump -types %t/packed.pdb > %t/packed-types.txt
RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-files-equal.py %t/orig-types.txt %t/packed-types.txt

Without the CodeView pack signature's leading pack list, an object is rejected,
and so is a pack list without the signature.
RUN: %python -c "d=bytearray(open(r'%t/orig/a.obj','rb').read()); i=d.find(b'.debug$T'); p=int.from_bytes(d[i+20:i+24],'little'); d[p:p+4]=(0x31505643).to_bytes(4,'little'); open(r'%t/bad.obj','wb').write(d)"
RUN: env LLD_IN_TEST=1 not lld-link /noentry /dll /nodefaultlib /debug \
RUN:   /out:%t/bad.dll %t/bad.obj 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BAD
BAD: invalid packed CodeView types in {{.*}}bad.obj: the type stream does not start with LF_CVPACK_LIST
RUN: %python -c "d=bytearray(open(r'%t/stage/a.obj','rb').read()); i=d.find(b'.debug$T'); p=int.from_bytes(d[i+20:i+24],'little'); d[p:p+4]=(4).to_bytes(4,'little'); open(r'%t/bad2.obj','wb').write(d)"
RUN: env LLD_IN_TEST=1 not lld-link /noentry /dll /nodefaultlib /debug \
RUN:   /out:%t/bad2.dll %t/bad2.obj 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BAD2
BAD2: invalid packed CodeView types in {{.*}}bad2.obj: LF_CVPACK_LIST in a type stream without the CodeView pack signature
